##You are given an integer array consisting of unique integers.
Originally, contained every integer within a certain range. However, some integers might have gone missing from the array.
The smallest and largest integers of the original range are still present in .
Return a sorted list of all the missing integers in this range. If no integers are missing, return an empty list.numsnumsnums#
class Solution:
    def findMissingElements(self, nums):
        minimum = min(nums)
        maximum = max(nums)

        result = []

        for i in range(minimum, maximum + 1):
            if i not in nums:
                result.append(i)

        return result
